    "title": "Patricia A. (Cahill) Ferranti",
    "text": "Patricia A. (Cahill) Ferranti, of Jamestown, 71, passed away Monday, Jan. 12, 2026.\nBorn in Providence, R.I., she was the daughter of the late Henry F. Cahill and the late Margaret A. (Johnson) Murphy.\nPatricia was the loving wife of Mark W. Ferranti, with whom she shared more than 47 years of marriage. Together, they had one daughter, Sarah M. Ferranti (husband, Ryan Lefaivre), whom Patricia lovingly described as her “greatest accomplishment.”\nOne of six children, Patricia is survived by her brothers, Scott A. Cahill and Kevin A. Cahill; her sister, Cheryl A. Desorcy; and many nieces and nephews. She was predeceased by her brothers, Henry F. Cahill and Raymond R. Cahill.\nPatricia lived a life defined by dedication, hard work, and a deep love for her family.\nThroughout her career, she brought that same care and commitment to everything she did — serving as a branch manager for Pawtucket Savings and Trust and co-owning The Baker’s Rack in North Kingstown alongside her childhood best friend, Christina Smith.\nPatricia also worked for the federal government, retiring after 20 years of service. At home, Patricia found her greatest happiness in the simple, meaningful moments: time spent with her family, baking and gardening. She will be remembered for her patience, kindness, quick wit, and strong work ethic, qualities that left a lasting impression on all who had the privilege of knowing her.\nPatricia’s services will be private.\nIn lieu of flowers, donations in Patricia’s memory may be made to the Breast Cancer Research Foundation (BCRF), 28 West 44th St., Suite 609, New York, NY 10036.\nKindly visit www.PatrickQuinnFuneralsandCremations.com for information and online condolences.",
